WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:21.180
As part of the celebration of International Spina Bifida and Hydrocephalus Day,

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:26.180
held every year starting on 25 October, the Ivorian Society of Neurosurgery,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:33.180
in association with the NGO Espérance's Hope, which fights hydrocephalus and neural tube defects,

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:39.180
has planned a collection of testimonies from parents living with children affected by these two conditions.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:46.180
This short film of about twenty minutes aims to raise awareness and help people better understand these two conditions,

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:53.180
as well as the means of prevention, to promote the rights of people affected by these conditions,

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:58.180
to encourage access to appropriate care and treatment,

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.180
and finally to fight the stigmatisation of these people.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:10.180
Spina bifida is this malformation of the nervous system that causes a deficiency in the back.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:16.180
At the level of the spine, the back part of the vertebrae does not fuse,

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:25.180
leaving an opening through which the nervous system, notably the spinal cord or the nerve roots, protrudes.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:33.180
This malformation, which is initially nervous tissue, causes an abnormality of the vertebrae,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.180
but also an abnormality of the skin.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:40.180
So the children are born with a lump on the back, or there is no lump,

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.180
but it looks like an open wound, and the skin is smooth and translucent.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.180
So this malformation is visible from birth.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:53.180
It is a malformation that is disabling,

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.180
very disabling, since the children are born with paralysis of the lower limbs,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:03.180
the paralysis cannot be reversed and the consequences cannot be treated,

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:08.180
notably sphincter problems: they urinate and pass stools without controlling it,

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:12.180
they sometimes also have foot malformations called clubfoot,

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.180
and it is very disabling; the care is very heavy,

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:22.180
since many specialists have to be involved: paediatricians, paediatric surgeons,

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:30.180
rehabilitation specialists, psychologists, urologists, so it is truly multidisciplinary,

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:34.180
and sometimes there are other malformations too: there can be heart malformations,

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.180
hydrocephalus, kidney malformations,

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.180
so it is a major malformation, but one that is compatible with life.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.180
Hello, Miss Assi,

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:54.180
today we have come to meet you at the headquarters of the NGO,

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.180
because World Spina Bifida and Hydrocephalus Day is coming soon,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.180
held every year on 25 October.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:10.180
We wanted to meet you in order to collect your testimony

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:15.180
and to have you share your daily life with us,

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:23.180
and how do you feel with a baby who has a similar condition?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:27.180
Hello Doctor, thank you for the opportunity you are giving us.
